     (decoder downmixing), or in the audio output (system mixer), this has no
     effect.

+``--audio-limit-downmix=<yes|no>``
+    Limit sample peaks when known-layout surround PCM is downmixed to mono or
+    stereo (default: no). Downmix in floating point, apply a linked look-ahead
+    limiter with a 0.95 ceiling and no automatic makeup gain, then convert to
+    the output format. The limiter compensates its look-ahead delay.
+
+    Stereo sources, multichannel outputs and passthrough are not processed.
+    Explicit ``--audio-normalize-downmix=yes`` retains the original normalized
+    matrix and disables this limiter. This does not repair clipping already
+    present in the source or guard against gain applied later by the output.
+
 ``--audio-resample-max-output-size=<length>``
     Limit maximum size of audio frames filtered at once, in ms (default: 40).
     The output size size is limited in order to make resample speed changes
